> Piecewise transforms and their knees

Inverse sRGB gamma uses v/12.92 below .04045 and
\(((v+.055)/1.055)^{2.4}\) above it. Lab uses
\(f(t)=t^{1/3}\) above \((6/29)^3\),otherwise
\(f(t)=t/[3(6/29)^2]+4/29\). Linear continuations avoid singular behavior
near black. Color operations use Float64;the prepared neural-network inputs
cast once to Float32. Native independent fixtures test both branches and knees.
```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/image_colorization_transfers.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  const auto x = n::arange(0., 1.001, .001, n::DType::Float64),
             small = n::arange(0., .03001, .0001, n::DType::Float64);
  auto a = dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), b = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  a.lines(x.to_vector<double>(), m::ColorLinearTensor(x).to_vector<double>(), "linear light",
          {37, 99, 235})
      .lines(x.to_vector<double>(), x.to_vector<double>(), "identity", {156, 163, 175})
      .title("Decode the sRGB transfer curve")
      .x_label("encoded sRGB v")
      .y_label("linear intensity")
      .y_limits(0, 1.3);
  b.lines(small.to_vector<double>(), m::ColorLabFTensor(small).to_vector<double>(), "Lab f(t)",
          {22, 163, 74})
      .title("Lab continues linearly near black")
      .x_label("white-normalized XYZ t")
      .y_label("piecewise f(t)")
      .y_limits(0, .4);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
  layout.add(a).add(b).size(1100, 480).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/image_colorization_transfers.svg");
  std::print("sRGB decode(.04045)={:.9f};Lab knee t={:.9f},f(t)={:.9f}.\n",
             m::ColorLinear(.04045), std::pow(6. / 29, 3), m::ColorLabF(std::pow(6. / 29, 3)));
}
```
