// result_end
\caption(Ninety-six visible complete-model Adam updates. Validation chroma MSE selects the checkpoint,with no held-out tuning or hidden fitting method.)
\alttext(Ninety-six visible complete-model Adam updates. Validation chroma MSE selects the checkpoint,with no held-out tuning or hidden fitting method.)


\image(figures/image_colorization_metrics.svg)
\caption(All32 held-out images compare learned chroma,neutral gray and the SGD-fitted constant. Chroma regression error and clipped-RGB PSNR measure different properties;all decoded images retain measured Lab lightness.)
\alttext(Held-out normalized chroma error and RGB reconstruction scores for learned and simple references.)

\image(figures/image_colorization_predictions.png)
\caption(All32 actual held-out images,two four-column tiles per row. Within each tile:grayscale,SGD-fitted mean chroma,learned colorization,original RGB. Nearest pixel scaling preserves the32px data.)
\alttext(Actual grayscale observations and their constant,learned and target colors,including weak/desaturated reconstructions.)

The learned model lowers test normalized ab MSE to .011777,compared with
.013745 for gray and .012040 for the SGD constant. Gray nevertheless has
higher RGB PSNR(26.589655 versus24.258774dB) and lower mean DeltaE76
(14.588410 versus14.956496). The learned output is still weakly colored;
its raw decoding places6.4972% of pixels outside the display gamut.

Regression cannot determine a unique color from lightness alone. The small
experiment reports its errors and out-of-gamut predictions without claiming
plausible semantic color recovery,Zhang-style classification,pretraining or
paper benchmark accuracy. More saturated output need not improve RGB scores.

> Conclusion

Physical Lab transforms,branch fixtures and complete Jacobians establish the numeric mechanism. Visible optimizers then fit both a constant reference and every CNN leaf on actual images. Restored lightness-only inference is immutable;the held-out comparisons show ambiguity,desaturation and differences between chroma and RGB error.

> References

- [Scikit-image v0.25.2 color conversion implementation](https://github.com/scikit-image/scikit-image/blob/v0.25.2/skimage/color/colorconv.py).
